<!--BlockDoc Documentation — LayerSeparation
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.target.blockdoc.documentation.LayerSeparation-->
<bddocumentation:LayerSeparation xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:bddocumentation="org.blockml.bml.target.blockdoc.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    BlockDoc vs compiler vs BOM vs other targets
  </is>
  <documentation>
    Layers relevant to BlockDoc:
    
    org.blockml.bml.bom.* (@blockml/bom) — Urmodell types BlockDoc reads (BlockDefinition,
    MemberDefinition, TypeExpression, CompositionTemplate, …).
    
    org.blockml.bml.target.blockdoc.* (this package) — path/link/page/site rules, options,
    RenderTarget contract for registry name blockdoc.
    
    @blockml/compiler — RenderTarget interface, CompileRequest, Target Registry, compileToOutput.
    Owns scope resolution (document|library|corpus|auto); BlockDoc only declares accepts[].
    
    @blockml/cli — bootstrapTargets from blockml.config.json targets[] (default ["blockdoc"]);
    writes RenderOutput files. Not part of this library.
    
    Sibling toolchain targets (xsd, fatblock) and domain targets (machineblocks-v3-scad)
    are separate packages with their own libraries.
  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="bddocumentation:ArchitectureOverview" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</bddocumentation:LayerSeparation>
